### Top Degrees for Aiding Vulnerable Populations

| Degree | Primary Job Titles | How They Directly Aid People |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Social Work (BSW/MSW)** | • Case Manager<br>• Medical Social Worker<br>• Clinical Social Worker | Connects people to housing, food stamps, and emergency resources. Provides mental health therapy. |
| **Human Services** | • Shelter Director<br>• Family Support Worker<br>• Youth Advocate | Manages community outreach programs and coordinates crisis intervention. |
| **Public Administration / Non-Profit Management** | • Non-Profit Director<br>• Community Organizer<br>• Program Manager | Secures grants, designs poverty-relief programs, and shapes policy. |
| **Public Interest Law (JD)** | • Legal Aid Attorney<br>• Tenant Advocate<br>• Public Defender | Prevents wrongful evictions and defends civil/human rights. |
